l behavior while preserving the upstream regression test added by this fix. No tests were run.", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T00:23:20.040707+00:00"}
{"commit": "1a791f4eee2dbb4e51f5211195a6f14da9aa5c12", "id": "1a791f4eee2dbb4e51f5211195a6f14da9aa5c12-1", "language": "rust", "reason": "Selected test is not present at the fixed revision: tests::test_request_path_backslash", "repo": "https://github.com/seanmonstar/httparse", "reproduction": {"attempt": "20260924T004721Z-dbd29894", "evidence_sha256": {"evidence/1a791f4eee2dbb4e51f5211195a6f14da9aa5c12-1/20260924T004721Z-dbd29894/origin.json": "6eaed53db326472c2651dbd3e2880f727bb240bfe78a89e57eb43e88d7030242", "evidence/1a791f4eee2dbb4e51f5211195a6f14da9aa5c12-1/20260924T004721Z-dbd29894/proposal.json": "5ab56de237cd1146b721300a81d0b3e4ea7b49f0b3afd884e92b442de6d1f57f"}, "provenance": "verbatim"}, "shard": "httparse", "status": "blocked", "subject": "Fix parsing backslashes in request-targets (#57)", "summary": "`is_uri_token` rejected `\\` even though RFC 3986 permits it in paths (and web clients routinely emit it). The fix removes the backslash exclusion from both the scalar check and the SIMD fast paths so backslash-bearing request targets round-trip through the parser.", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T00:47:21.149608+00:00"}
{"commit": "59a9fd11b3023581055b4997ff21829e03e909a2", "id": "59a9fd11b3023581055b4997ff21829e03e909a2-1", "language": "rust", "reason": "Selected test is not present at the fixed revision: tests::test_request_header_value_htab", "repo": "https://github.com/seanmonstar/httparse", "reproduction": {"attempt": "20260924T005256Z-e10ce402", "evidence_sha256": {"evidence/59a9fd11b3023581055b4997ff21829e03e909a2-1/20260924T005256Z-e10ce402/origin.json": "e906aa4c8f1966e2e15ce9311ce76a75b75641418279ccdbbb3ac0757cc73e75", "evidence/59a9fd11b3023581055b4997ff21829e03e909a2-1/20260924T005256Z-e10ce402/proposal.json": "1020b2d4a9d6f36603f793285575f3b274f0bec61e7444259a30b4a49681a0e6"}, "provenance": "verbatim"}, "shard": "httparse", "status": "blocked", "subject": "allow htabs in header values", "summary": "`HEADER_VALUE_MAP` omitted HTAB (`0x09`), so header values containing tabs \u2014 explicitly permitted by RFC 7230 \u2014 were rejected as invalid. The fix adds HTAB to the allowed set alongside `0x20..=0x7E` and `0x80..`.", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T00:52:56.341075+00:00"}
