c1c49fb7cdd6b63edde99af"}, "failure": "tests::test_method_within_buffer panicked: assertion failed: REQUEST.as_ptr() <= method.as_ptr()", "fixed_commit": "6e7ba52a860685b740daf537f24ff56792ed9170", "fixed_tree": "e44095548e0dd62690de26975a79d41062cd5e00", "fixes": [{"commit": "6e7ba52a860685b740daf537f24ff56792ed9170", "parent": "fbb0bdde72a9b571ded779fdc3544d8a39c812fc"}], "patch": "patches/6e7ba52a860685b740daf537f24ff56792ed9170-1/20260924T204811Z-f0067188.patch", "provenance": "verbatim", "restored_source_matches": true, "runs": {"buggy": {"exit_code": 101, "log": "evidence/6e7ba52a860685b740daf537f24ff56792ed9170-1/20260924T204811Z-f0067188/buggy.log", "named_result": "FAILED", "tests_run": 1, "timed_out": false}, "fixed": {"exit_code": 0, "log": "evidence/6e7ba52a860685b740daf537f24ff56792ed9170-1/20260924T204811Z-f0067188/fixed.log", "named_result": "ok", "tests_run": 1, "timed_out": false}, "restored": {"exit_code": 0, "log": "evidence/6e7ba52a860685b740daf537f24ff56792ed9170-1/20260924T204811Z-f0067188/restored.log", "named_result": "ok", "tests_run": 1, "timed_out": false}}, "signature": "assertion failed: REQUEST.as_ptr() <= method.as_ptr()", "test_sources": [{"commit": "6e7ba52a860685b740daf537f24ff56792ed9170", "paths": ["src/lib.rs"]}], "tests": ["tests::test_method_within_buffer"]}, "shard": "httparse", "status": "confirmed", "subject": "fix: return method string from buffer (#136)", "summary": "The GET and POST parsing fast paths returned static string literals instead of slices of the request buffer. The fix returns the consumed method bytes from that buffer, excluding the trailing space. The regression test added by the fix checks that a parsed GET method points within the input buffer. Both reversal regions occur exactly once in their respective revisions and contain only implementation code. No tests were run; the failing pointer-bound assertion depends on memory layout.", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T20:51:16.622361+00:00"}
{"commit": "498de3fa707a4889395850e88e8260261258bbd2", "id": "498de3fa707a4889395850e88e8260261258bbd2-1", "language": "rust", "reason": "Selected test is not present at the fixed revision: tests::test_request_with_invalid_token_delimiter", "repo": "https://github.com/seanmonstar/httparse", "reproduction": {"attempt": "20260925T171911Z-bc675945", "evidence_sha256": {"evidence/498de3fa707a4889395850e88e8260261258bbd2-1/20260925T171911Z-bc675945/origin.json": "d956e519b30562ac7bee1f96258f468a97d1ee2a245868274a8e44c6b4fa41e0", "evidence/498de3fa707a4889395850e88e8260261258bbd2-1/20260925T171911Z-bc675945/proposal.json": "222ae7ba568802c37e8899ba82e8cdb5cb411c98042ea6fbb30145985d50473a"}, "provenance": "verbatim"}, "shard": "httparse", "status": "blocked", "subject": "stop parsing requests with invalid method or path delimiters", "summary": "`parse_token` terminated on SP, CR, or LF, so `\"GET\\r / HTTP/1.1\"` parsed successfully with method `\"GET\"` even though the method/path boundary must be a single SP. The fix restricts the terminator to SP, causing any other non-token byte to error.", "updated_at": "2026-09-25T17:19:11.950402+00:00"}
{"commit": "c0631f26e86157a8110a202c112b0ea7a051025b", "id": "c0631f26e86157a8110a202c112b0ea7a051025b-1", "language": "rust", "reason": "Selected test is not present at the fixed revision: tests::test_response_no_cr", "repo": "https://github.com/seanmonstar/httparse", "reproduction": {"attempt": "20260925T171926Z-281ee532", "evidence_sha256": {"evidence/c0631f26e86157a8110a202c112b0ea7a051025b-1/20260925T171926Z-281ee532/origin.json": "20d0fcfa9be84b0ab5c9f3ed8be283d14bb4027907b93ac375a3f6461de9a0a1", "evidence/c0631f26e86157a8110a202c112b0ea7a051025b-1/20260925T171926Z-281ee532/proposal.json": "a9a5751c2b50912d54c3ec6215103782393a783d3a7a1f163ad0881aef1555a4"}, "provenance": "verbatim"}, "shard": "httparse", "status": "blocked", "subject": "Fix parsing responses that have no reason phrase followed by no CRs (#96)", "summary": "When the status line ended in bare LF with no reason phrase, `Response::parse` set `reason = Some(\"\")` without advancing the byte-slice cursor, so the next header-name slice started inside the status-line digits (producing names like `\"200\\nContent-type\"`). The fix calls `bytes.slice()` to snap the cursor before parsing headers.", "updated_at": "2026-09-25T17:19:26.367547+00:00"}
